The bug: `n` was set to `len(queries)+1`, but the binary search operates on `sums`, which has `len(nums)+1` entries. With mismatched lengths (e.g., `nums=[4,5,2,1]`, `queries=[3,10,21]`), the search range capped at `r=len(queries)+1=4`, so query `21` returned `3` instead of `4`. Setting `n = len(nums)+1` makes `r` the correct exclusive upper bound; re-tracing `queries=[3,10,21]` yields `[2,3,4]`, and edge cases (`q` smaller than all sums → 0, `q` ≥ total sum → `len(nums)`, exact-match `break`) all check out.

